    stem: "The Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) of two integers a and b is the largest number that divides into both with no remainder. One of the oldest and most famous algorithms was first described by Greek mathematician, Euclid, in his book of Elements written around 300BC. The code snippet below is an implementation of Euclid’s algorithm using subtraction to find the GCD of 45 and 18.",
